In drug discovery, quantum computers could be used to simulate the behavior of molecules at the atomic level, allowing researchers to design new drugs with greater precision and efficiency. In finance, quantum computers could be used to optimize investment portfolios and predict market trends more accurately. And in materials science, quantum computers could be used to design new materials with unique properties, such as superconductors that operate at room temperature.
