TALLINN – The city government of the Estonian city Tartu and the European Investment Bank (EIB) signed a 20 million euro framework loan agreement that will support the city's investments into education.

Through this financing, the EIB expresses its support for small to medium-sized education investments, and small-size municipal infrastructure schemes in Tartu. Under the scheme, the municipality will use the fund for renovations of basic schools and, at a later stage, high schools as well. In line with the climate priorities that the European Investment Bank has adopted, the investmentMUST be included. 

