USER: I have an HTML page with many unnecessary tags. I want to clean up the HTML code by removing all the unnecessary tags. 
Here is the HTML code:
Website

Heading
=======


This is a paragraph.
* Item 1
* Item 2
* Item 3


Copyright © 2021


What is the best way to remove all the unnecessary tags and clean up the HTML code? Please provide the code in [JavaScript code] format.

ASSISTANT: Here's a JavaScript code that removes the unnecessary tags and cleans up the HTML code:
```javascript
const html = `
Website

Heading
=======


This is a paragraph.
* Item 1
* Item 2
* Item 3


Copyright © 2021


`;
const parser = new DOMParser();
const doc = parser.parseFromString(html, "text/html");
// Remove unnecessary tags
doc.head.remove();
doc.body.removeAttribute("class");
doc.querySelector("div.container > header").remove();
doc.querySelector("div.container > footer").remove();
// Get the cleaned up HTML code
const cleanedUpHtml = doc.documentElement.outerHTML;
console.log(cleanedUpHtml);
```
The output will be:
```html

This is a paragraph.
* Item 1
* Item 2
* Item 3

``` <|endoftext|>

