Gracias por el consejo pero esta pregunta esta bien en este foro pienso porque no se como llevar los datos del formulario shipping address y billing address que peternecen al objeto Account que provee la API de salesforce y asi obtener su latitud y longtiud para luego marcar el mapa.

ok, entiendo. No estaba muy claro en tu pregunta. Espero que la respuesta de david te ayudo.

You can add a marker to a Leaflet map like this:
var m = L.marker([latitude, longitude], { 'title': 'Title' })
     .bindPopup('Title')
     .addTo(map)
     .on('click', function(e) {
         // React to a click
     }); 

That gets you a map marker with a popup, and the opportunity to execute a callback function on click.
Leaflet does not, itself, provide geolocation services. You must have the latitude and longitude you wish to display before you create the map marker.
You can use a geocoding service within Salesforce to automatically populate geolocation fields, but it's not synchronous. When you save your Accounts from Visualforce, you won't instantly get back geocode information. Additionally, geocoding does not support custom address fields; it will only populate geocodes for the standard addresses on the Account. See the Salesforce documentation and release notes for more about setting up geocoding.
Alternately, you can make a callout yourself to your preferred geolocation service to obtain the latitude and longitude corresponding to your address data (before or after saving records), and supply that information to Leaflet.

