@ricardo-valero this is a good first issue if you are interested exploring further.
The record update is parsed into roc_parse::ast::Expr::RecordUpdater and then de-sugared in crates/compiler/can/src/desugar.rs. It's pretty much all contained to one pattern match in desugar_expr, and a fun place to see how the front end of the compiler AST is handled.
Initial Workload Name has to be parameterised


The initial/default workload name is hard coded in the locals variables as "Workload1".
It would be helpful to make it as variable that customer can feed in.
If the customer realises this hard-coded name after the LZ is configured, it would be hard to modify the code and re-run TF later. The reason is that it would raise other terraform errors related to SCH, storage buckets and it would be difficult to troubleshoot.


